          "id": "ch2_liberalism_sec_11",
          "title": "Marxism",
          "start_page": 18,
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "page": 18,
              "text": "\"Workers of the world, unite! You have nothing to lose but your chains!\" - Karl Marx Marxism, encapsulated in this rallying cry by Karl Marx, is a socio-political and economic theory that has profoundly influenced the course of history. Emerging in the midst of the tumultuous 19th century, Marxism was a response to the challenges and inequalities brought about by the Industrial Revolution and the rise of capitalism. This ideology, forged in the crucible of social upheaval, has since evolved, diversified, and sparked revolutions, all while serving as a critical lens for understanding class struggle, power dynamics, and societal transformation."
            }
          ],
