              "id": "ch3_marxism_b38",
              "page": 26,
              "label": "Economic Equality",
              "text": "Eliminates extreme disparities by ensuring equal access to resources , contrasting the wealth concentration in capitalism. \"In a country where the sole employer is the state, opposition means death by slow starvation.\" – Leon Trotsky (cautioning against state overreach) From Socialism to Communism During the socialist phase , the state manages production and redistribution. As class distinctions fade , the state loses its relevance and gradually withers away . \"The government of persons is replaced by the administration of things.\" – Friedrich Engels",
              "full_text": "Economic Equality : Eliminates extreme disparities by ensuring equal access to resources , contrasting the wealth concentration in capitalism. \"In a country where the sole employer is the state, opposition means death by slow starvation.\" – Leon Trotsky (cautioning against state overreach) From Socialism to Communism During the socialist phase , the state manages production and redistribution. As class distinctions fade , the state loses its relevance and gradually withers away . \"The government of persons is replaced by the administration of things.\" – Friedrich Engels"
