              "id": "ch3_marxism_b80",
              "page": 37,
              "label": "",
              "text": "Habermas developed the theory of the public sphere and communicative action, advocating for deliberative democracy and civic participation within an ideal speech situation. He believed that meaningful participation in civic affairs should involve open and rational discourse among citizens. This, in turn, would foster a more inclusive and democratic society.",
              "full_text": "Habermas developed the theory of the public sphere and communicative action, advocating for deliberative democracy and civic participation within an ideal speech situation. He believed that meaningful participation in civic affairs should involve open and rational discourse among citizens. This, in turn, would foster a more inclusive and democratic society."
