              "label": "Global Vision",
              "text": "Gandhi's universal values of nonviolence and justice addressed global concerns, positioning his thought as both rooted and cosmopolitan. Gandhi’s critique was not anti-modern but ethical and human-centric , offering a model of modernity that upholds self-reliance, sustainability, and spirituality over industrial excess and moral erosion.",
